    "slug": "ssc-comprehensive-guide",
    "title": "SSC Recruitment 2026 | Complete Guide to SSC CGL, CHSL, CPO & All Exams",
    "keyword": "SSC Recruitment 2026 | Complete Guide to SSC CGL, CHSL, CPO & All Exams",
    "description": "Complete SSC recruitment guide 2026. SSC CGL, CHSL, CPO, Stenographer, eligibility, salary ₹25K–₹35K, selection process, success rates (0.3%), and 2,347+ live job opportunities across India.",
    "content": "<div class=\"container\">\n        <div class=\"stats\">\n            <div class=\"stat-box\">\n                <div class=\"stat-number\">2,347</div>\n                <div class=\"stat-label\">Total Live Opportunities</div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat-box\">\n                <div class=\"stat-number\">0.3%</div>\n                <div class=\"stat-label\">Success Rate</div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat-box\">\n                <div class=\"stat-number\">₹25K–₹35K</div>\n                <div class=\"stat-label\">Entry Salary Range</div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat-box\">\n                <div class=\"stat-number\">2.3M</div>\n                <div class=\"stat-label\">Applications (Recent Cycle)</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <h2>1. SSC Overview</h2>\n        <p>The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) is a central government recruitment agency responsible for recruiting staff for various ministries and departments. SSC conducts multiple competitive exams every year to fill vacancies for Group B and Group C positions across the country. With 2,347+ posts available this year, SSC offers the largest volume of government job opportunities in India.</p>\n\n        <h2>2. Exam Types: CGL, CHSL, CPO, Stenographer, MTS</h2>\n        <p><strong>SSC CGL (Combined Graduate Level):</strong> 2,347 posts, Bachelor's degree required, ₹25K–₹35K entry salary. Includes Assistant, Statistician, Inspector roles. Success rate: 0.3%.</p>\n        <p><strong>SSC CHSL (Combined Higher Secondary Level):</strong> 456 posts, 12th pass required, ₹21K–₹30K entry. Postal Assistant, Clerk roles.</p>\n        <p><strong>SSC CPO (Central Police Organization):</strong> 156 posts, Bachelor's degree, ₹35K–₹45K entry, Physical test required for police roles.</p>\n        <p><strong>SSC Stenographer:</strong> 234 posts, 12th pass, shorthand typing skill required, ₹21K–₹30K.</p>\n        <p><strong>SSC MTS:</strong> 89 posts, 10th pass, ₹18K–₹25K entry, easiest SSC exam.</p>\n\n        <h2>3. Salary &amp; Career Progression</h2>\n        <table>\n            <tbody><tr>\n                <th>Position</th>\n                <th>Entry (Year 1)</th>\n                <th>Year 10</th>\n                <th>Year 20+</th>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td>SSC CGL</td>\n                <td>₹27,000</td>\n                <td>₹65,000</td>\n                <td>₹90,000+</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td>SSC CHSL</td>\n                <td>₹21,000</td>\n                <td>₹55,000</td>\n                <td>₹65,000+</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td>SSC CPO</td>\n                <td>₹35,000</td>\n                <td>₹75,000</td>\n                <td>₹100,000+</td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody></table>\n\n        <h2>4. Eligibility Requirements</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Nationality: Indian citizen</li>\n            <li>Age: 18–32 years for SSC CGL (with relaxation for SC/ST/OBC/PWD up to 37–42 years)</li>\n            <li>Education: Bachelor's degree for CGL, 12th pass for CHSL, 10th for MTS</li>\n            <li>Character: No criminal record required</li>\n            <li>Physical Fitness: Medical fitness certificate</li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <h2>5. Selection Process</h2>\n        <p><strong>Tier 1 (Preliminary):</strong> 60-minute online MCQ test, 200 marks, qualifying round only.</p>\n        <p><strong>Tier 2 (Main):</strong> 200 marks, main exam that counts toward final merit list.</p>\n        <p><strong>Tier 3 (Descriptive):</strong> 100 marks, essay/application writing (for CGL only).</p>\n        <p><strong>Tier 4 (Skill Test):</strong> Typing test for Data Entry Operator, Stenographer roles.</p>\n        <p><strong>Document Verification:</strong> Final step after qualifying all tiers.</p>\n\n        <h2>6. FAQ</h2>\n        <div>\n            <p><strong>Q: What's the success rate in SSC?</strong><br>\n            A: SSC CGL has 0.3% success rate (1 out of 333 applicants selected). This makes it highly competitive but with better odds than UPSC (0.08%).</p>\n\n            <p><strong>Q: How long to prepare for SSC?</strong><br>\n            A: Typical preparation: 6–12 months for CGL. Daily 4–6 hours of study recommended.</p>\n\n            <p><strong>Q: Can I apply for multiple SSC exams?</strong><br>\n            A: Yes! No restriction. Many apply for CGL, CHSL, and CPO simultaneously.</p>\n\n            <p><strong>Q: What's pension in SSC jobs?</strong><br>\n            A: 50% of last salary. SSC officer retiring with ₹70K salary = ₹35K/month pension for life.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <h2>7. Live Opportunities</h2>\n        <p><strong>Current Active Postings:</strong> 2,347 posts across all SSC exams and departments.</p>\n        <ul>\n            <li>SSC CGL: 2,347 posts (largest volume)</li>\n            <li>SSC CHSL: 456 posts</li>\n            <li>SSC CPO: 156 posts</li>\n            <li>SSC Stenographer: 234 posts</li>\n            <li>SSC MTS: 89 posts</li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <p><strong>Browse Related Hubs:</strong><br>\n        <a href=\"/hubs/upsc-comprehensive-guide.html\">UPSC Guide</a> |\n        <a href=\"/hubs/banking-comprehensive-guide.html\">Banking Jobs</a> |\n        <a href=\"/hubs/delhi-comprehensive-guide.html\">Delhi Jobs</a> |\n        <a href=\"/hubs/maharashtra-comprehensive-guide.html\">Maharashtra Jobs</a></p>\n    </div>",
